        "committer": {
          "name": "Yonatan Nachum",
          "email": "ynachum@amazon.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 16:37:54.000000000",
          "tz": 0
        },
        "subject": "LU-20791 efalnd: Skip deactivating connections on lookup",
        "message": "LU-20791 efalnd: Skip deactivating connections on lookup\n\nA deactivated connection stays in the hash table under key 0 until the\nconnection daemon reaps it, and keeps its remote NID. A lookup for a\npeer whose key falls in the same bucket still matches it, so the caller\ngets the dead connection back and refreshes its use time. A send then\nleaves its message pending on it until the daemon cancels it, without\nstarting a new connection, and a probe from that peer is rejected.\n\nThe impact is limited since the daemon removes the connection from the\nhashtable at first scan and then cancel all pending messages which\ncauses a retry of the message.\n\nSkip connections in the deactivating state on lookup, checking the state\nunder the connection lock.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nChange-Id: I051097b746292950c80c5441aca79efe7538e3e0\nSigned-off-by: Yonatan Nachum <ynachum@amazon.com>\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
